  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 300 AM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nTwo areas of cyclonic circulation were noted on water vapor imagery \nat 08Z, one over eastern IA and the other over far southeast CO. A \ntrough axis between the two low pressure systems is approaching the \nforecast area early this morning. Precipitation appears unlikely due \nto fairly weak mid-level ascent and a lack of saturation in the \ncolumn as the trough moves over the area today, but rain could occur \nboth to the north and south. Cloud cover, however, makes it way back\nover the area today, with low stratus impacting northeast KS. After \nstarting the day in the upper 30s to near 40 degrees, temperatures \nwill be limited to the mid 50s this afternoon.\n\nFriday will be a chilly day as a surface ridge builds in from the \nnorth. Some locations in north-central KS could dip into the mid 30s \ntonight/Friday morning, while locations to the east will be slightly\nwarmer. Temperatures are then only expected to reach the low 50s for\nhighs. A warming trend commences this weekend and continues into \nearly next week as southerly and westerly flow returns. Models are in\ngood agreement with highs around 70 degrees by Monday afternoon. \nTemperatures remain around 70 and conditions stay dry through at \nleast midweek.",
